Maximum Data Burst Volume (MDBV). MDBV denotes the largest amount of data that the 5G-AN is required to serve within a period of 5G-AN PDB (i.e. 5G-AN part of the PDB). The MDBV may be signalled with 5QIs to the (R)AN, and if it is not received, a standardized value applies (for standardized 5QIs the value in the QoS characteristics Table 5.7.4 applies). Observation 2: The Maximum Data Burst Volume is for Delay Critical GBR QoS Flow only, but it does not mean it shall always be signlled to RAN. The current TS 38.413 and the other spec where QoS parameters are deifned has the below strucutre or similar: The above table contains the 6 QoS characteristics defined by SA2 and has been well discussed. It is specified that “Maximum Data Burst Volume is specified in TS 23.501,” where the presence etc of the IE is well specified already. Proposal 1 RAN3 to agree not to change the presence of the Maximum Data Burst Volume IE. Proposal 1 RAN3 to agree not to change the presence of the Maximum Data Burst Volume IE.

